From bca5629f389d54d1e553e0bf6cee50f2dd006f52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:56:20 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 61/70] core: a scene health report (WPENGINE_HEALTH)

A scene that loads and draws something can still have lost a layer, an effect or a script on the way (3414858021
lost its head's compose layer to four glslang errors for months, and nothing outside the log said so). With
WPENGINE_HEALTH=<path> set when a project loads, the core appends JSON lines saying what it built and what it
left out: one `object` record per scene object (built or not; an unbuilt image's scene-data box), `dropped` /
`effect_dropped` with the reason, `shader_error` (glslang or GL, vertex / fragment / link), `missing_asset`
(texture, font, model, puppet, particle, material, sound, shader module), `script_error` (layer, property,
phase), `unsupported` features LWE logs as such, the HLSL-lenient rewrites in use (`compat`), and each drawable's
canvas bbox, alpha and transform finiteness at render frames 1 and 31 (`layers`). Thread-local scopes (object,
effect, shader) name the layer an error deep in a shader compile belongs to. Off by default: every call site is
one relaxed atomic load; nothing the renderer does depends on it.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/reports/scene-health.md (the per-scene health report)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
